WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Forget everything you think you know about cats. A new generation of scientists is challenging preconceptions.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Cat research is definitely lagging behind the dog, but now we're seeing an explosion of cat science.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Genetics wise, you basically have a wild animal living in your house. Yes, they have their attitude, but if you want, you can teach a cat to do anything.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:34.000
The saying is that cats always land on their feet. They first have to recognize where their body is in space using a phenomenon known as the righting reflex.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Kristin has done extensive research on what cats want. She gives cats a choice, and more than half the time, they choose their people.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Cats in the Middle Ages were associated to witches, and they had cats to get rid of rodents. There came the time when the church tried to get rid of them. Thankfully, even during these dark times, some people continued to nurture a bond with cats.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:13.000
They seem to be able to insert frequencies that overlap with the frequencies that a human baby makes when it cries.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:19.000
One benefit of whiskers: they tell a cat how small a hole she can fit through.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:26.000
If you want your cat to like you, one of the very first things you can do is the slow blink.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Join us as we solve the mysteries of the cat, decode their crazy antics, and decipher their hidden language. Anyone can unlock a cat's true potential if you learn their secrets.